※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1 run=native,qemu exit=12 diag=none

※ What a macro writes is expanded in turn, so a macro may write another one -- and
※ an argument is expanded after the invocation holding it, so a macro is handed
※ what the caller wrote including any invocation nested in it.
※
※ Both happen here: `outer` writes an invocation of `twice`, and `twice` is handed
※ one of `three` that the caller wrote.

macro three:
    ⌜⌝ → ⌜3u8⌝

macro twice:
    ⌜$x⌝ → ⌜$x + $x⌝

macro outer:
    ⌜$x⌝ → ⌜twice⌜$x⌝⌝

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    ⎕narrow(outer⌜three⌜⌝⌝ × 2u8, ⌜u6⌝) ?? 1u6
